<header class="ref-head yr-head"><p class="cty-kicker">Year by year · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p><h1 class="research-title">963 CE</h1><p class="ref-lede">963 CE in world history: 4 events, 1 birth, 2 deaths, 2 states founded and 1 that came to an end. 390 recorded states existed that year.</p></header>
<nav class="ref-letters yr-near" aria-label="Nearby years"><a href="/years/958">958 CE</a><a href="/years/960">960 CE</a><a href="/years/961">961 CE</a><a href="/years/962">962 CE</a><a href="/years/963" aria-current="page">963 CE</a><a href="/years/965">965 CE</a><a href="/years/966">966 CE</a><a href="/years/968">968 CE</a><a href="/years/969">969 CE</a></nav>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/nikephoros-ii-phokas" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nikephoros-ii-phokas.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-16">16 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Nikephoros II Phokas is crowned Byzantine emperor</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nikephoros-ii-phokas">Nikephoros II Phokas</a> was crowned emperor, swearing to protect the two sons of the late Romanos II, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/basil-ii">Basil II</a> and Constantine VIII, who were already co-emperors. He was murdered by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-i-tzimiskes">John Tzimiskes</a> in 969.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nikephoros-ii-phokas">Nikephoros II Phokas</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/otto-i" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/otto-i.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/november-6">6 November</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Otto I convenes a synod in Rome to depose Pope John XII</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Under the authority of Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otto-i">Otto I</a>, a possibly uncanonical synod met in Saint Peter's Basilica to depose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-john-xii">Pope John XII</a>, who had crowned Otto emperor in 962, for armed rebellion against him. The synod sat until 4 December.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otto-i">Otto I</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-john-xii">Pope John XII</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/st-peters-basilica">St. Peter's Basilica</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/otto-i" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/otto-i.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-6">6 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Leo VIII claims the papacy with the backing of Otto I</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Leo VIII, a Roman prelate appointed by Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otto-i">Otto I</a>, was ordained a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> and claimed the Holy See in opposition to John XII. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catholic-church">Catholic Church</a> counts him an antipope until 23 June 964 and the legitimate pope thereafter.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otto-i">Otto I</a></div></div></li></ol></section>
